    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d11-a3">

                <pb facs="0052" n="42" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg42"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Consulate,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-12-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 15, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I herewith forward to you an official copy
                    of the register of the priva teer Scylla, or Rappahannock. You will notice that
                    she stands this day regis tered at the proper department of the English revenue
                    service as a British ship. There has been no legal transfer, and the legal
                    ownership at 3 o’clock this day was in Robert Gordon Coleman, No. 28 Clement’s
                    lane, London. So far, then, as the true ownership is shown by the papers
                    required to make a legal transfer, she is a British privateer under the rebel
                    flag.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>English boiler-makers from Sheerness, and other mechanics, are still at work
                    fitting her out, and seamen are almost daily sent to her from this country in
                    small numbers at a time.</p>
                <p>I remain, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. H. MORSE, <hi rendition="#italic">Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">United States Minister at London.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
